<title>UK: Scottish TV plans name change.</title>
<headline>Scottish TV plans name change.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scottish T.V. Plc plans to change its name to Scottish Media Group after expanding into newspaper publishing, the company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>STV, the ITV company for central Scotland, acquired Glasgow-based Caledonian Publishing for 120 million stg last October. Caledonian publishes The Herald and The Evening Times.</p>
<p>The proposed name change will be put to the company's Annual General Meeting on May 2.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
